1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,967
Prism Scan checks your watchlist with your own Sets.

2
00:00:03,419 --> 00:00:08,199
On the left are your saved Sets, like the Pullback in an uptrend Set we just built.

3
00:00:08,249 --> 00:00:12,090
Tap plus, or drag one across, and it becomes a Prism Scan.

4
00:00:12,536 --> 00:00:16,522
Each scan is a card. The top row shows its answers and controls.

5
00:00:16,542 --> 00:00:18,532
Open it to see the details.

6
00:00:18,988 --> 00:00:23,853
Choose what it scans. Groups like All crypto follow your watchlist as it changes.

7
00:00:24,302 --> 00:00:28,805
Press play to check every asset now, on the latest finished daily candles.

8
00:00:28,855 --> 00:00:32,995
Or rewind to a past moment, and Prism rebuilds what was known then.

9
00:00:33,045 --> 00:00:36,502
Here, the fifteenth of January 2024.

10
00:00:38,810 --> 00:00:42,993
Each asset gets Yes, No, or Unknown, with the line that decided it.

11
00:00:43,455 --> 00:00:45,035
That's a good start.

12
00:00:45,085 --> 00:00:46,980
But crypto tends to move together,

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,188
and many traders only buy a dip when Bitcoin itself is in an uptrend.

14
00:00:51,238 --> 00:00:52,946
Let's add that check.

15
00:00:53,402 --> 00:00:56,731
In Signal Sets, open the Set and add My Trend again,

16
00:00:56,781 --> 00:00:59,620
this time pinned to a fixed asset: Bitcoin.

17
00:00:59,670 --> 00:01:03,234
Then add a third line: My Trend on Bitcoin is Bullish.

18
00:01:11,492 --> 00:01:15,397
Save it as version two. The earlier version stays as it was.

19
00:01:15,839 --> 00:01:19,360
Back in Prism, the scan shows a newer version is available.

20
00:01:19,410 --> 00:01:21,182
One tap switches it.

21
00:01:21,643 --> 00:01:23,031
Run it again.

22
00:01:23,081 --> 00:01:26,858
Now a dip is only a Yes when Bitcoin's own trend is bullish too.

23
00:01:26,908 --> 00:01:29,619
When it isn't, the Bitcoin line is the reason.

24
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:34,146
To keep watching, give the scan a schedule. Here, every daily close.

25
00:01:34,608 --> 00:01:36,807
Then choose how you hear about it:

26
00:01:36,857 --> 00:01:38,138
instantly,

27
00:01:38,188 --> 00:01:39,789
in the daily summary,

28
00:01:39,839 --> 00:01:41,590
or only in the app.

29
00:01:42,054 --> 00:01:47,239
Collapse all keeps a long list tidy. That's Prism: descriptive readings, not advice.
